    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="0615" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123.R27/70.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 18, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mrs. Reid’s decision is very gratifying to the Department. Two battleships will
                    meet the British ship off Nantucket.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
